Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:45:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] camera: USB camera VDI on the x86 emulator's vivid
 capture node

From harmony-contrib/ohos-qemu (patches/common/drivers/peripheral/camera),
which runs the same OpenHarmony-7.0-Release code on upstream device/qemu:

- usb_backend 0001: camera_hal is no longer emptied on an x86_64 product
  that is not is_emulator when the USB camera VDI is selected
  (drivers_peripheral_camera_feature_usb).
- vivid_capture 0001/0002 + qemu_v4l2_capture.h: the new feature
  drivers_peripheral_camera_qemu_vivid_capture lets the V4L2 enumerator
  accept the kernel's vivid driver (not only uvcvideo) and checks the
  node's own device_caps for streaming capture.
- jpeg_capture 0001-0005: advertise and produce JPEG captures by
  software-encoding the YUYV frames, select the capture pipeline, and
  default the optional photo quality.
- jpeg_rotation 0001: initialise the libjpeg transform options.
- fork_timestamp 0001: propagate the frame timestamp to the photo.

Everything is behind the two feature flags; the phones do not use the
USB camera VDI.

Change-Id: I9bb1f7e3513cc7320f7a4a7208deebb0ab33a41a
Signed-off-by: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
